  "limitations": [
    "One 10462 story with two characters, 960x540 preview and this container’s software Mesa device; not a benchmark across every scene, computer or GPU.",
    "A brief compile overlapped portions of historical runs, and shader/disk caches can differ. Warm samples reduce startup effects but do not create a fully controlled hardware benchmark.",
    "Do not promise a fixed 30 fps: this device measured approximately 20 fps in the paired optimized sample and 24 fps in the later run. Persistent playback keeps wall-clock timeline progress by skipping presentation frames while executing required simulation steps.",
    "The final export resolution, supersampling and temporal evaluation are not reduced by these preview optimizations.",
    "Linux mouth checks use an explicitly labeled actual-PCM amplitude fallback because this fixture has no CRI weights and no Linux MotionSync library. Windows native MotionSync requires the separate real Windows CI gate.",
